text:
The question of whether a dependency merits inclusion is, in my view, best approached by weighing its long-term obligations against its immediate convenience, since the former are typically underestimated at the moment of adoption. Before adding any package, I would recommend writing a short tutorial or minimal working example that exercises only the functionality one actually requires; this exercise frequently reveals whether a few dozen lines of local code would suffice, and it also documents the integration for future maintainers.

Considerations worth recording include:

- maintenance activity and release cadence;
- licence compatibility and transitive footprint;
- the cost of eventual removal.

